# 2. PLATFORM ARCHITECTURE

Build three integrated components sharing one authoritative cloud database.

## A. Android mobile application

Recommended stack:

- Kotlin
- Jetpack Compose
- Material 3
- Room local database
- Android WorkManager for background synchronisation
- Camera and document/photo selection
- GPS location capture, subject to permissions
- Digital signature capture
- Secure API communication

The application must support Android phones and tablets, including devices used in mining environments with poor or intermittent connectivity.

## B. Secure cloud backend

Recommended stack:

- Supabase with PostgreSQL, Auth and private object storage; or an equivalent production-grade backend.
- REST APIs or an equivalent typed API layer.
- Database migrations, access policies, audit logging and background jobs.
- Server-side validation and role-based authorisation.

Use a single authoritative database for customers, sites, users, assessments, photographs, signatures, equipment, documents, chemical records, remedial actions and reports.

Never place privileged backend keys, service-role keys, database passwords or other secrets in the Android application or public web frontend.

## C. Web-based management portal

Recommended stack:

- Next.js
- React
- TypeScript
- Responsive desktop and mobile layouts
- Secure backend API integration
- Role-protected administrative screens

The portal must provide full management functionality, not merely display a dashboard. Authorised users must be able to maintain customer records, assign assessors, manage sites, configure checklist templates, review assessments, upload laboratory results, approve reports and export documentation.

All three components must use the same records, permissions, workflow statuses and audit history.

