# 11. OFFLINE-FIRST AND CLOUD SYNCHRONISATION

Fieldwork must remain possible without internet connectivity.

The Android application must:

1. Download the assessor's authorised assignments and required reference data.
2. Save draft assessments locally in Room.
3. Save answers, remarks and attachment metadata locally.
4. Retain photographs and signatures securely until synchronisation succeeds.
5. Queue pending uploads and database changes.
6. Retry failed synchronisation automatically when connectivity returns.
7. Display clear Offline, Pending Sync, Syncing, Synced and Sync Failed states.
8. Provide a manual retry option.
9. Preserve user changes when a request fails.
10. Detect conflicting edits and provide an auditable resolution process.

Use stable UUIDs and idempotent server operations to prevent duplicate records.

Do not delete local evidence until the server has confirmed that the upload and associated record changes were successfully committed.

Define a conflict policy. For example, conflicting edits to submitted or approved assessments must not silently overwrite one another. Preserve both versions or require an authorised resolution.

The web portal must show the latest successfully synchronised information and identify records that have not yet reached the cloud.

